rowhammer (0.36.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Make --reset non-destructive (user decision): instead of deleting a
    file it is moved to <file>-YYYYMMDDhhmmss.bak next to it, so a reset
    can be undone with a single mv. One timestamp is used for the whole
    run, so the backups of a "--reset all" belong together visibly.
  * Wait for the next second when a backup of the current second already
    exists (the same reset ran twice in a row): sleep 1, take a fresh
    timestamp and retry rather than overwrite the backup just written.
    After RESET_STAMP_ATTEMPTS (3) tries the reset gives up with a
    message instead of looping on a stuck clock.
  * Spell the reset question "[N/y]" so the declining default is visible
    in the prompt itself.
  * Add --force (ROWHAMMER_FORCE): answer confirmation questions with
    "yes" instead of asking. Combines with any other option and is
    without effect where nothing is asked, so the game starts normally
    with it; today it covers the --reset question.

