rowhammer (0.29.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Stop dropping highscore entries that predate a counter field (user
    decision): loading the list used to require all ten fields and
    discarded any shorter line outright, so every time a counter was
    appended to the format (gold/silver in 0.4.0, play time in 0.5.0,
    rowhammers in 0.6.0, pieces in 0.7.0) older rounds silently vanished
    the next time the file was loaded and re-saved. highscore_load now
    accepts the field counts the format actually passed through since
    the 0.4.0 scoring rebuild (5, 7, 8, 9 or 10 fields) and fills in 0
    for whichever trailing counters a line does not carry. Lines from
    before that rebuild (leading "score" field, "rows" third) use a
    different column order rather than a shorter version of the
    current one and are still dropped, since reusing their fields
    under the current layout would misassign the old score as rows.

