rowhammer (0.28.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Center the main menu and every other menu, info screen and prompt in
    the terminal, so they line up with the play screen (centered since
    0.22.0) instead of clinging to the top left corner.
  * All those screens are now built as plain content lines and placed by
    render_menu_frame (lib/render.sh): it aligns them with the left edge
    of the game block, centers them vertically on their own height and
    erases what a previous screen left behind. A menu following another
    menu only rewrites the rows involved, so browsing a menu does not
    flicker; a menu following the play screen, the resize overlay or the
    echoed name prompt clears the terminal first.
  * A resize repaints menus and info screens from their lines instead of
    re-emitting the stored frame, which now carries absolute cursor
    positions valid only for the size they were computed from.
  * Info screens gained one body line (MENU_BODY_MAX), because the
    frames no longer spend a row on clearing the top screen line.

