rowhammer (0.27.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Count the pieces a round places and show them as "Pieces" in the
    HUD, below the play time (user request).
  * Highscore list and statistics gain the piece count ("PCS") and the
    placement rate derived from it and the play time ("PPM", pieces per
    minute); the statistics also show the all-time pieces, the total
    play time and the resulting rate.
  * Both tables were exactly at the 48-column minimum width, so an
    entry now spans two lines (explicitly allowed by the user). That
    gives the highscore name 12 characters again instead of 6, and it
    makes the screens taller than a 22-row terminal: the highscore list
    is paged (five entries per page, table head repeated), and the
    statistics split into all-time counters and recent rounds.
  * File formats change accordingly (no backward compatibility, per the
    project rule - old lines simply fail validation and are dropped):
    highscore entries gain a trailing "pieces" field, recent-round
    entries gain "pieces" and "time" before the date, and the
    statistics file gains the "pieces" and "play_time" counters.
  * A round without a single cleared row is banked into the statistics
    from now on: it still carries pieces and play time, which the
    all-time placement rate needs.

