rowhammer (0.21.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add configurable colors via named color themes. A theme maps every
    piece type and the gold/silver squares to symbolic color names, each
    carrying a basic (8/16-color ANSI) and an extended (xterm 256-color)
    meaning. Four themes ship: "guideline" (the previous default look,
    unchanged), "classic", "mono" and "colorblind" (deuteranopia-friendly).
    Selectable in the settings menu (with a live per-theme color swatch),
    via --color-theme NAME and the ROWHAMMER_COLOR_THEME environment
    variable, and persisted to the user config file (COLOR_THEME).

