rowhammer (0.20.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Cleared rows now blink before they vanish: when a lock completes one
    or more rows, those rows flash twice (highlighted / normal, about
    280 ms in total) and only then are removed and the next piece
    spawns. The rows are collected before the clear (board_full_rows),
    the renderer highlights them via FLASH_ROWS/FLASH_STATE and
    flash_rows drives the animation; duration and cycle count are
    adjustable via FLASH_MS/FLASH_CYCLES (FLASH_CYCLES=0 disables it).
    Square detection still runs first, so a row through a freshly built
    gold/silver square flashes at its full value.

